<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T5.20" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A5.T5.21" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">POPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> results on MSCoco <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> and A-OKVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, for Llava <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. In both datasets, ReCo provides a significant performance boost to all the methods (where <span id="A5.T5.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Original</span> stands for the unmodified Llava).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
