</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>CHAIR</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A5.T7" title="In E.2 CHAIR ‣ Appendix E More quantitative results ‣ ReCo: Reminder Composition Mitigates Hallucinations in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we depict the improvement that ReCo offers over all baselines in the generative task of image description, when the underlying VLM is LlaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Similar to the observations of the main text, ReCo reduces both CHAIR<sub id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">s</span></sub> and CHAIR<sub id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i</span></sub>, especially as the output length increases, with the improvement being as high as <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>33</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">33\%</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T7.27" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A5.T7.28" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">CHAIR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> results for Llava <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. <span id="A5.T7.28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Original</span> stands for the unmodified VLM, while VCD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, M3ID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, and AvisC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> are the three baselines we consider. In all four cases, the addition of ReCo improves significantly the performance as the generation progresses, reducing CHAIR<math id="A5.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>s</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> as much as <math id="A5.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44\%</annotation></semantics></math> and CHAIR<math id="A5.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>i</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.T7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>33</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">33\%</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32,\ 64,\ 128,\ 256,\ 512,\ \text{and }1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 128</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 256</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 512</mn><mo rspace="0.627em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32,\ 64,\ 128,\ 256,\ 512,\ \text{and }1024</annotation></semantics></math> standing for the maximum allowed number of generated tokens.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T7.29" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
